---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Line of Sight, Angle of Elevation & Depression | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn line of sight, angle of elevation, angle of depression, and their geometric properties for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Applications of Trigonometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">01</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 01 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Line of Sight, Elevation & <span>Depression</span></h1>
					<p>
						Understand the fundamental concepts of heights and distances: line of sight, angle of elevation (looking up), and angle of depression (looking down).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · DEFINITIONS -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · KEY DEFINITIONS</div>
					<h2>Core Concepts & Terminology</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Line of Sight</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Line of Sight</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">The straight line drawn from the eye of an observer to the object viewed.</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Elevation</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Angle of Elevation</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">The angle formed by the line of sight with the horizontal line when looking <strong>UPWARD</strong> (object above horizontal level).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Depression</span>
							<div>
								<p><strong>Angle of Depression</strong></p>
								<span style="color:#64748b; font-size:14px;">The angle formed by the line of sight with the horizontal line when looking <strong>DOWNWARD</strong> (object below horizontal level).</span>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- SVG Visualizing Angle of Elevation & Depression -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">GEOMETRIC DIAGRAM</span>
							<h3>Angle of Elevation vs Angle of Depression</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="340" height="220" viewBox="0 0 340 220" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">
									<!-- Top Horizontal Line -->
									<line x1="40" y1="40" x2="300" y2="40" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
									<text x="50" y="30" fill="#64748b" font-size="12" font-weight="700">Horizontal (Top)</text>

									<!-- Bottom Horizontal Line -->
									<line x1="40" y1="180" x2="300" y2="180" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
									<text x="190" y="196" fill="#64748b" font-size="12" font-weight="700">Horizontal (Ground)</text>

									<!-- Line of Sight (Diagonal) -->
									<line x1="40" y1="180" x2="300" y2="40" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3"/>
									<text x="120" y="125" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" transform="rotate(-28, 120, 125)">Line of Sight</text>

									<!-- Vertical Line (Tower) -->
									<line x1="300" y1="40" x2="300" y2="180" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="3"/>

									<!-- Angles Arcs -->
									<!-- Angle of Elevation arc -->
									<path d="M 85 180 A 45 45 0 0 0 80 159" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="92" y="174" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="900">θ (Elevation)</text>

									<!-- Angle of Depression arc -->
									<path d="M 255 40 A 45 45 0 0 0 260 61" stroke="#e11d48" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="185" y="30" fill="#e11d48" font-size="12" font-weight="900">θ (Depression)</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<div class="calc-box">
								Key Property: <strong>Angle of Elevation = Angle of Depression</strong> (Alternate Interior Angles)
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · TRIGONOMETRIC RATIOS FOR HEIGHTS & DISTANCES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · RATIOS TO USE</div>
					<h2>Selecting the Right Ratio</h2>
					<p>
						In right-angled triangle problems:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>tan θ = Opposite (Height) / Adjacent (Distance)</strong>
						<strong>sin θ = Opposite (Height) / Hypotenuse (Slant Length / String)</strong>
						<strong>cos θ = Adjacent (Distance) / Hypotenuse (Slant Length)</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Always draw a clear right triangle diagram first!</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Angle of elevation = Angle of depression because horizontal lines are parallel.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p><strong>tan 30° = 1/√3</strong>, <strong>tan 45° = 1</strong>, <strong>tan 60° = √3</strong> (Most frequently used values!).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>OVERVIEW</small>
								<strong>Chapter Overview</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/single-triangle-problems" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Single Right Triangle Problems</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">APPLICATIONS OF TRIGONOMETRY</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 01 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 25%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/line-of-sight-elevation-depression" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Line of Sight & Angles</strong>
									<small>Elevation & depression rules</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/single-triangle-problems" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Single Triangle Problems</strong>
									<small>Height & distance calculations</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/double-triangle-problems" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Double Triangle Problems</strong>
									<small>2-triangle NCERT word problems</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
		.lesson-page {
			min-height: 100vh;
			background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f8fbff 0%, #ffffff 35%, #f7f9fc 100%);
			color: #14213d;
			padding: 45px 0 100px;
		}

		.lesson-container {
			width: min(1120px, calc(100% - 40px));
			margin: 0 auto;
		}

		.back-link {
			display: inline-flex;
			align-items: center;
			gap: 7px;
			color: #667085;
			text-decoration: none;
			font-size: 14px;
			font-weight: 700;
			margin-bottom: 35px;
			transition: color 0.2s ease, transform 0.2s ease;
		}

		.back-link:hover {
			color: #2563eb;
			transform: translateX(-3px);
		}

		.lesson-header {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 80px minmax(0, 1fr);
			gap: 25px;
			align-items: center;
			padding: 40px;
			border: 1px solid #e1e7f0;
			border-radius: 24px;
			background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
			box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(20, 33, 61, 0.055);
			margin-bottom: 45px;
		}

		.lesson-number {
			width: 80px;
			height: 80px;
			display: flex;
			align-items: center;
			justify-content: center;
			border-radius: 20px;
			background: #eef4ff;
			color: #2563eb;
			font-size: 23px;
			font-weight: 900;
		}

		.lesson-label {
			color: #2563eb;
			font-size: 11px;
			font-weight: 850;
			letter-spacing: 1.7px;
			margin-bottom: 10px;
		}

		.lesson-header h1 {
			margin: 0;
			font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 54px);
			line-height: 1.05;
			letter-spacing: -2px;
			font-weight: 900;
			color: #14213d;
		}

		.lesson-header h1 span {
			color: #2563eb;
		}

		.lesson-header p {
			margin: 15px 0 0;
			max-width: 720px;
			color: #687180;
			font-size: 17px;
			line-height: 1.65;
		}

		.content-layout {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px;
			gap: 45px;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.lesson-content {
			min-width: 0;
			padding: 5px 0 0;
		}

		.topic-label {
			color: #2563eb;
			font-size: 11px;
			font-weight: 900;
			letter-spacing: 1.8px;
			margin-bottom: 14px;
		}

		.second-label {
			margin-top: 60px;
		}

		.lesson-content h2 {
			margin: 0;
			color: #14213d;
			font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 38px);
			line-height: 1.1;
			letter-spacing: -1.5px;
			font-weight: 900;
		}

		.lesson-content > p {
			max-width: 780px;
			margin: 18px 0 0;
			color: #687180;
			font-size: 16.5px;
			line-height: 1.75;
		}

		.formula-box {
			margin-top: 22px;
			padding: 24px 28px;
			border-radius: 20px;
			background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a 0%, #1e293b 100%);
			color: #ffffff;
